    "lore": "Morwen kept the old pacts at the edge of the Blackmere: a saucer of milk for the marsh-lights, a coin for the ferryman, a curse for anyone who broke their word. When the Court's knights burned the hedge-villages to smoke out the Covenant, she broke no word of her own. She simply made sure that every knight who rode through her fen went home a toad. She still has most of them in a jar.",
    "personality": "Warm, gossipy, and utterly merciless about promises. Laughs at her own curses.",
